Recents grouped by day, the way the sessions list reads in Hermes
=================================================================

The rail was one flat "Recent" block capped at thirty-five rows. That answers *what did I touch most
recently* and nothing else. The question a person asks their own history is *what was I doing on
Tuesday*, and the day is the unit they ask it in.

So: Pinned first, then one group per calendar day of the conversation's last activity, newest day
first, each header carrying its own count — `TODAY 19`, `YESTERDAY 8`, `Monday · Nov 1 3`. Inside a day,
newest activity first. The grouping is local time, so it agrees with the clock on the wall rather than
with UTC.

Measured against the real session files on this machine: Today 19, Yesterday 8.

